    "summary": "Added \u00a711's economy to the pure ledger. Content: ruinGold 40, supplyCacheGold 25, rumorPrice 25, tonicPrice 30, tonicTicks 240, tonicCarryLimit 2 in objectiveRules, plus grantAmount/itemPrice and GOLD_GRANT_REASONS/SHOP_ITEMS; the validator is extended and a test refuses a negative price and a carry limit of 0. Simulation: new economy.ts with grantGold (keyed: ruin per player+key, supply-cache per key match-wide; duplicate/already-claimed), purchase (request ids unique; a matching repeat returns the original record with replayed:true and the same state, even at a stale tick; a mismatched reuse is duplicate; refusals insufficient-gold, player-in-duel, player-disconnected, player-left, tonic-limit), useTonic/activeTonic (active on ticks start..start+239; refusals tonic-active, no-tonic, not-at-sea, grappled, player-in-duel, player-disconnected). State gains goldSpent, grants, purchases, and per-player tonics/tonicEffect. Leaving drops tonics; a duel loss keeps them. The invariant is now balances + goldSpent = goldIssued, with grant-key uniqueness, grant amounts, purchase-id uniqueness, the purchases summing to goldSpent, and tonic bounds. Scripted tests in ledger.test.ts use the Run harness, which gained an optional rules argument. Property tests add an economy stream on its own seeded dice, interleaved so the existing sequences and their coverage are unchanged, with per-step gold and tonic checks and 23 new EXERCISED entries. docs/objectives.md has an Economy section. Checks run in this worktree after npm ci: npm run typecheck, npm run test:unit (644 passed), npm run test:integration (36 passed) and npm run build (smoke passed), all exit 0.",
